# One DDR input pin and two DDR output pins, stated as `ddr` attributes on
# the ports in the design. `rx` is two bits on one pin, bit 0 captured on
# the rising edge of `clk` and bit 1 on the falling one; `tx` is four bits
# on two pins the same way. The iCE40's SB_IO registers both edges
# itself, so each pin is one SB_IO with the DDR PIN_TYPE and nothing else.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 clk 21
create_clock -name sys -period 40.0 clk
